probe-flat-stall-stop: a replica patch to Evan Daniel's search/exact/exactsolve.py at the
pin vendor/evand-regularize/vendored.yaml records (think-ux1v). devtools.regularize_evand
applies it to a copy of search/exact in its scratch replica, never to vendor/, and only on
the retry ladder's rung for a solve that ran out of time; vendor/evand-regularize/README.md
(Local Changes) says why, and devtools.check_vendored_evand checks that it still applies
to the pinned bytes.

probe_flat, the realization test of the zero modes, runs Gauss-Newton per mode and sign
until the residual is below 10^-(dps-20) or for 40 iterations. Redundant contacts that
meet tangentially floor the residual near 1e-39, as upstream's own comment anticipates,
so the 1e-60 stop is never reached: at n = 290 every one of 78 modes spent all 80
least-squares solves, about 30 s a mode, and the solve ran out of 1,800 s. The patch also
stops once the residual is below 1e-34 and fell less than tenfold in the last step. The
acceptance test (residual < 1e-30, correction < 1e3 t^2, |dS| < 1e-30) is unchanged, the
probe works on copies of the point, and neither the KKT point nor the certificate depends
on it: at n = 18 both are byte-identical with and without the patch, and at n = 290 the
solve certifies in 222 s at upstream's published S'.

